{
  "name": "A/B/C exhaustive: every input combination, then every single-bit walk",
  "_notes": [
    "Drives the adversarial logic cases. A=0x642 bit32, B=bit33, C=bit34.",
    "Each combination is held for 40 ms (20 cycles), long enough for any",
    "one- or two-cycle pipeline to settle, then the walk section changes one",
    "bit at a time so edge-triggered logic is exercised as well as levels.",
    "The 'C held' section is load-bearing: a stale read of an intermediate term is INVISIBLE unless that term changes while the other operand is already asserted, or the two change in the same step. A trace that only walks one bit at a time between long holds will pass a wrongly-ordered config."
  ],
